From 3503833b7322bceaec003849e6f46f81e45d28fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Martin=20=C5=A0trobl?= <recordyletsplays@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:19:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] a3y17lte: Use the mainline kernel's WWAN ports

The mainline driver for the modem of the Exynos7870 exposes two WWAN
ports, Samsung IPC ("SIPC") and the remote file system channel
("SIPC-RFS"), and starts the modem itself when the IPC port is opened.

Give the a3y17lte device its own transport: find the ports by type in
sysfs and use them, without boot code. If there are none, the kernel
provides the vendor driver's interface and the herolte code is used as
before. Packet data contexts are WWAN links that userspace creates; they
are expected to be named rmnetN, like the vendor kernel's.

Setting LIBSAMSUNG_IPC_FRAME_LOG to a file name appends every message
in both directions to it as a line of hex, to record what the modem
sends.
